{% from 'ingressroute.yml.j2' import ingressroute with context %}
{#
  Public as well as LAN, which is the macro's default — so this call passes no `public`
  argument at all.

  It was `public=false` until 2026-08-24, on the reasoning that the reference pages map every
  service, hostname, auth tier and backup posture, and that a complete map of the homelab
  should not face the internet. That reasoning was retired deliberately, not overlooked: the
  operator asked for a name reachable off the LAN, and the map is only as exposed as the gate
  in front of it.

  What makes that safe is that the gate covers EVERY path. There is one route, matched on the
  Host rule alone, and `bypass_prefixes` is empty — so `/healthz` and `/build-info.json` sit
  behind Authelia on the public name exactly as the pages do. Adding a bypass prefix here
  would put an unauthenticated endpoint on the internet; there is no reason to want one, since
  the readiness probe dials the pod directly and never traverses this route.
#}
---
{{ ingressroute(
    container_item.name,
    container_item.hostname | default(container_item.name),
    container_item.port,
    container_item.use_authelia,
  )
}}
